## Milestone B (Week 2): Paid voting and tick finalization (end-to-end)
Deliverables:
- Users can submit a paid vote for a direction during a tick window.
- Aggregator resolves winner at tick end.
- `finalizeTick()` posts result onchain.
- Client moves cursor once per tick based on finalized result.

Acceptance criteria:
- From two separate wallets:
  - cast votes on different directions in the same tick
  - see one move applied
  - see pot increase with each vote
- Cursor position is consistent for all viewers.

Owner mapping:
- Intern 1: contract vote storage + finalizeTick logic
- Intern 2: aggregator tick loop + winner selection + chain submission
- Intern 3: client shows tick countdown, submits votes, listens to tick events

---

## Milestone C (Week 3): Timeout + claim pot
Deliverables:
- Timeout resets after each finalized tick move.
- If no finalized move occurs for TIMEOUT duration, last mover can claim pot.
- Claim transfers funds and starts a fresh round (or resets pot to 0).

Acceptance criteria:
- After TIMEOUT:
  - only last mover can successfully claim
  - pot becomes 0 (or rolls to treasury, depending on rules)
  - UI updates immediately

Owner mapping:
- Intern 1: claim logic + tests
- Intern 2: aggregator handles “no votes” ticks cleanly
- Intern 3: client claim UX + status messages

